 481:./segger-rtt/src/SEGGER_RTT_printf.c **** 
 482:./segger-rtt/src/SEGGER_RTT_printf.c **** /*********************************************************************
 483:./segger-rtt/src/SEGGER_RTT_printf.c **** *
 484:./segger-rtt/src/SEGGER_RTT_printf.c **** *       SEGGER_RTT_printf
 485:./segger-rtt/src/SEGGER_RTT_printf.c **** *
 486:./segger-rtt/src/SEGGER_RTT_printf.c **** *  Function description
 487:./segger-rtt/src/SEGGER_RTT_printf.c **** *    Stores a formatted string in SEGGER RTT control block.
 488:./segger-rtt/src/SEGGER_RTT_printf.c **** *    This data is read by the host.
 489:./segger-rtt/src/SEGGER_RTT_printf.c **** *
 490:./segger-rtt/src/SEGGER_RTT_printf.c **** *  Parameters
 491:./segger-rtt/src/SEGGER_RTT_printf.c **** *    BufferIndex  Index of "Up"-buffer to be used. (e.g. 0 for "Terminal")
 492:./segger-rtt/src/SEGGER_RTT_printf.c **** *    sFormat      Pointer to format string, followed by the arguments for conversion
ARM GAS  C:\Users\PRAETE~1\AppData\Local\Temp\ccGZ7q0H.s 			page 32


 493:./segger-rtt/src/SEGGER_RTT_printf.c **** *
 494:./segger-rtt/src/SEGGER_RTT_printf.c **** *  Return values
 495:./segger-rtt/src/SEGGER_RTT_printf.c **** *    >= 0:  Number of bytes which have been stored in the "Up"-buffer.
 496:./segger-rtt/src/SEGGER_RTT_printf.c **** *     < 0:  Error
 497:./segger-rtt/src/SEGGER_RTT_printf.c **** *
 498:./segger-rtt/src/SEGGER_RTT_printf.c **** *  Notes
 499:./segger-rtt/src/SEGGER_RTT_printf.c **** *    (1) Conversion specifications have following syntax:
 500:./segger-rtt/src/SEGGER_RTT_printf.c **** *          %[flags][FieldWidth][.Precision]ConversionSpecifier
 501:./segger-rtt/src/SEGGER_RTT_printf.c **** *    (2) Supported flags:
 502:./segger-rtt/src/SEGGER_RTT_printf.c **** *          -: Left justify within the field width
 503:./segger-rtt/src/SEGGER_RTT_printf.c **** *          +: Always print sign extension for signed conversions
 504:./segger-rtt/src/SEGGER_RTT_printf.c **** *          0: Pad with 0 instead of spaces. Ignored when using '-'-flag or precision
 505:./segger-rtt/src/SEGGER_RTT_printf.c **** *        Supported conversion specifiers:
 506:./segger-rtt/src/SEGGER_RTT_printf.c **** *          c: Print the argument as one char
 507:./segger-rtt/src/SEGGER_RTT_printf.c **** *          d: Print the argument as a signed integer
 508:./segger-rtt/src/SEGGER_RTT_printf.c **** *          u: Print the argument as an unsigned integer
 509:./segger-rtt/src/SEGGER_RTT_printf.c **** *          x: Print the argument as an hexadecimal integer
 510:./segger-rtt/src/SEGGER_RTT_printf.c **** *          s: Print the string pointed to by the argument
 511:./segger-rtt/src/SEGGER_RTT_printf.c **** *          p: Print the argument as an 8-digit hexadecimal integer. (Argument shall be a pointer to
 512:./segger-rtt/src/SEGGER_RTT_printf.c **** */
 513:./segger-rtt/src/SEGGER_RTT_printf.c **** int SEGGER_RTT_printf(unsigned BufferIndex, const char * sFormat, ...) {
